{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-4a7b-8c9d-0e1f2a3b4c5d",
		"name": "SMTrack API - Backend",
		"description": "Postman collection for **Smart Meter GPS Tracking System Backend** (Express + TypeScript + Prisma).\n\nBase URL: `{{baseUrl}}` (default `http://localhost:3001`).\n\n## How to use\n1. Import this collection in Postman.\n2. Set environment variable `baseUrl` (collection variable already set).\n3. Run **Auth → Login (Admin)** once — the test script automatically saves `accessToken` and `refreshToken` as collection variables. All protected routes then use `{{accessToken}}` in the `Authorization` header.\n4. IDs (userId, trackerId, geofenceId, notificationId) are auto-captured by test scripts when you create/fetch resources.\n5. Collection variable `randEmail` is regenerated per run via pre-request scripts so the register test can be repeated.\n\n## Roles\n- ADMIN / MANAGER / FIELD_ENGINEER — enforced via `authorize()` middleware.\n- Seeded users (after `npm run prisma:seed`): admin@smtrack.com / admin123, manager@smtrack.com / manager123, engineer@smtrack.com / engineer123.\n\nRate limit: 100 requests / 15 min per IP — keep an eye while running the whole collection.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
		"_exporter_id": "smtrack"
	},
	"variable": [
		{ "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:3001" },
		{ "key": "accessToken", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "refreshToken", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "userId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "trackerId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "geofenceId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "notificationId", "value": "" },
		{ "key": "randEmail", "value": "test.user@example.com" }
	],
	"auth": {
		"type": "bearer",
		"bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
	},
	"item": [
		{
